2. LIFECYCLE STATE MACHINE
============================================================

Implement the lifecycle state machine defined by:

docs/shared-memory-architecture-v1.md

Use the existing canonical states.

Expected conceptual lifecycle:

CREATED
   ↓
ACTIVE
   ↓
EXPIRED
   ↓
ARCHIVED
   ↓
DELETED

But DO NOT blindly assume these transitions.

Use the architecture specification and Sprint 1 implementation
as the source of truth.

Every transition must be explicitly validated.

Invalid transitions must produce a typed lifecycle error.

Examples:

ACTIVE → EXPIRED
ACTIVE → ARCHIVED
ARCHIVED → DELETED

may be valid depending on the specification.

But transitions such as:

DELETED → ACTIVE

must never silently succeed.

